  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">

      <div class="csec">
        <h2>What Training actually does in FC Mobile</h2>
        <p>Training is the system that improves an individual player's in-game stats and gameplay — things like pace, shooting, or passing attributes. It's separate from Rank Up, which is the only thing that raises a player's OVR and Team OVR. Mixing these two up is the single most common reason first-time players feel like their coins or cards "disappeared" with nothing to show for it.</p>
        <p>To train a player, you feed other player cards into them as Training XP (TXP). Each training level requires a set amount of TXP, and the cost climbs steeply as the level gets higher — level 1 only needs 100 TXP, but level 30 alone needs 16,000. That's why the calculator above adds up every level in between rather than just the start and end points.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="csec">
        <h2>Training vs. Rank Up: what's the difference?</h2>
        <table class="compare-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Training</th><th>Rank Up</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Currency used</td><td>Other player cards (TXP)</td><td>Rank Up Points</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Affects OVR?</td><td>No</td><td>Yes, +1 OVR per rank</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Affects stats?</td><td>Yes — this is its whole job</td><td>Indirectly, via Skill Points</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cap</td><td>Training Level 30</td><td>5 ranks per player</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="csec">
        <h2>How to get the most out of every card you spend</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Bronze (47–59 OVR) and Silver (60–69 OVR) cards give the cheapest XP per coin — keep a stash instead of buying them one at a time mid-training.</li>
          <li>Higher OVR cards give more XP per card but cost far more in coins, so they're rarely worth using purely as training fodder.</li>
          <li>If you've already trained a player and want to move that progress elsewhere, use Training Transfer — just remember it only passes on 90% of the XP, a 10% loss applies automatically.</li>
          <li>TOTY, Icon, and some promo cards can need more TXP per level than a standard card at the same OVR — always check the exact cost shown on the training screen before committing.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="csec">
        <h2>TXP required per level</h2>
        <p>The full Season 26 table the calculator above pulls from — useful if you'd rather plan by hand or double-check a specific level.</p>
        <div class="ref-grid">
          <div class="ref-panel">
            <h3>TXP per training level</h3>
            <p class="sub">Level 1 through the level 30 cap.</p>
            <div class="ref-table-scroll">
              <table class="ref-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>TXP</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="fullTxpTable"></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ref-panel">
            <h3>Card XP value by OVR</h3>
            <p class="sub">What a card is worth when melted for training.</p>
            <div class="ref-table-scroll">
              <table class="ref-table">
                <thead><tr><th>OVR band</th><th>XP value</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="xpValueTable"></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="csec">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div id="faqList"></div>
      </div>

    </div>
